+## Textual realization
+
+Before literal/regex show on realized flow/root, collapse adjacent spaces to one
+occurrence whose newline origin is the OR of its components. Discard only an
+inferred newline occurrence when an adjacent internal textual character satisfies
+the pure pinned Unicode nonspacing classification (Han/Bopomofo/Hiragana/Katakana/
+Yi and the measured ideographic punctuation, not Korean or ambiguous curly quotes).
+Use immutable data and the authorized icu_properties dependency; codex's unavailable
+space_discarding module is not an import substitute. Keep explicit space between
+supporting texts when no component has newline. Explicit Linebreak is destructive
+and consumes adjacent spaces, including explicit ones, but remains Linebreak.
+Parbreak and actual nontext content remain causal boundaries. A textless style
+wrapper does not hide adjacent characters for normalization; distinct style
+chains do separate regex matching groups. Do not use global trim/split_whitespace,
+document language or target-specific space heuristics.
+
+Search literal/regex over the largest eligible realized group of the same lexical
+snapshot and style chain, including separated Text/space and dynamic text nodes.
+Each recipe receives only its matched slice; preserve leftmost order, unmatched
+prefix/suffix, precedence, guard/revocation and depth limit. A replacement is not
+fed back into the same revoked rule. Empty regex matches remain rejected and
+literal '.' stays distinct from regex '.'.
+
+While a ContentBlock is only a value, preserve raw Space/SpaceFromNewline.
+Its local textual show operates provisionally before normalization: replace only
+the matched slice, preserving unmatched separators for later insertion. Root
+realization normalizes the inserted value and applies its eligible snapshot.
+The combined local CJK show/normalization case and sequential-identical-rule
+override remain explicit unresolved parity obligations, not presumed successes.
